      "url": "/events/library-3d-printing-for-teens-2026-07-29/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Curious about 3D printing?",
      "text": "Curious about 3D printing?\n\nLearning\n\n3D Printing for Teens\n\nCurious about 3D printing?\n\nAbout this event\n\nCurious about 3D printing? Join us for a hands-on class that introduces the basics of 3D design using TinkerCAD, a free and beginner-friendly web-based program. Learn how to create simple 3D models and see how designs are brought to life with a 3D printer. No experience needed - just bring your creativity! This series is for teens in grades 7-12 (as of fall 2026). Registration is required; participants must attend all four days of the series. This program is made possible through the generous support of New York-Presbyterian. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nWednesday, July 29, 2026\n\nTime\n\n1:00 PM - 2:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\n3D Printing for Teens\n\nJul 30, 2026\n\nCurious about 3D printing?\n\nTell Your Story: Zine-Making for Teens\n\nJul 1, 2026\n\nExplore how artists, writers, and designers use zines (ZEENS) to communicate ideas through words, images, and layout.\n\nTell Your Story: Zine-Making for Teens\n\nJul 2, 2026\n\nExplore how artists, writers, and designers use zines (ZEENS) to communicate ideas through words, images, and layout."
