      "text": "It&#39;s Am erica&#39;s 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran&#39;s life,…\n\nLearning\n\nAm erica 250: The Importance of Revolutionary War Pensions\n\nIt's Am erica's 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran's life,…\n\nAbout this event\n\nIt's Am erica's 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran's life, family, and service. This program shares how to find pensions, the information often available, and interpretation tips that are helpful to genealogists and researchers alike! Presented in collaboration with Ruth Keeler Memorial Library, White Plains Public Library, Eastchester Public Library and The Field Library. Registration is required. Click Here To Register. Click Here to Join the Zoom Directly. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, June 23, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED\n\nGeorge Washington Carver: Genius Behind The Peanut Man\n\nJun 18, 2026\n\nBorn in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century.\n\nThe Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 25, 2026\n\nLearn about why the 1776 approval of the Declaration of Independence, specifically at the White Plains court house, was such a big deal for New York and…"
