      "text": "The evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nLearning\n\nComité Noviembre: Reception\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nAbout this event\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments. The event is free but registration is required. Comit&eacute; Noviembre is a NY-based organization committed to preserving, honoring, and celebrating the deep cultural roots and lived experiences of the Puerto Rican diaspora in New York, across the U.S., and on the island. The exhibit will be on view in the Library's Museum Gallery through September 1. &iexcl;Que Viva Puerto Rico! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nThursday, July 16, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:45 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nSummer Reading Kickoff featuring Jumpin' Jamie!\n\nJun 27, 2026\n\nCome start your summer vacation at the White Plains Public Library!\n\nREVOLUTIONARY SOUNDS!\n\nJul 2, 2026\n\nRevolutionary Sounds explores the rich cultural exchange between European and African music in colonial New York.\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED"
