      "text": "The premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including…\n\nLearning\n\nFuture is Female\n\nThe premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including…\n\nAbout this event\n\nThe premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including Dorothy Sayers and Agatha Christie, form a secret society to solve a real murder, in order to prove they are equal to men in a male-dominated literary world. This book is available through our catalog in the Library's physical collection and as both an ebook and audiobook in Libby. To join, Click This Zoom Link. You can also use the following phone number to call in: +1 929 436 2866 US (New York). Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nMonday, September 14, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nSustainable Westchester\n\nAug 26, 2026\n\nFor more information contact Daniel Zitomer, Program Coordinator/Energy Advisor at 914-242-4725 ext 114 or daniel@sustainablewestchester.org\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nSep 17, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED"
