      "excerpt": "A Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York&#39;s jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.",
      "text": "A Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York&#39;s jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.\n\nCivic\n\nJazz at Noon: Vanisha Gould\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.\n\nAbout this event\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally. Her acclaimed albums In Her Words (2021), Life's a Gig (2024) and She's Not Shiny, She's Not Smooth (2024) center women's experiences with wit and honesty. In 2023, she received The Jazz Gallery Composition Residency Commission, advancing her work in large-scale, interdisciplinary performance. Visit Website Watch on You Tube Check out the full Jazz Fest White Plains lineup here! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nFriday, September 25, 2026\n\nTime\n\n12:00 PM - 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPre Fall Season Meeting and Clinic on New Laws of the game\n\nAug 26, 2026\n\nSponsored by the Westchester Soccer Referee Organization.\n\nShort Story Film Discussion Series\n\nJun 25, 2026\n\nJoin White Plains Librarian Barbara Wenglin to explore compelling readings from the rich anthology, Music Stories (ed.\n\nSCORE Meeting\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nMonthly SCORE Chapter Meeting."
