      "text": "SENIORS 60+ MAY QUALIFY FOR FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE ARE YOU STRUGGLING TO KEEP UP WITH HOUSING EXPENSES?\n\nLearning\n\nNYSOFA Grant for Seniors\n\nSENIORS 60+ MAY QUALIFY FOR FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE ARE YOU STRUGGLING TO KEEP UP WITH HOUSING EXPENSES?\n\nAbout this event\n\nSENIORS 60+ MAY QUALIFY FOR FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE ARE YOU STRUGGLING TO KEEP UP WITH HOUSING EXPENSES? Westchester Residential Opportunities, Inc. (WRO) may be able to assist with: Rental Arrears Utility Arrears Delinquent Mortgage Payments Delinquent HOA Condominium/Co-op Fees Property Taxes If you are behind on housing-related expenses, assistance may be available to help you preserve your housing stability and avoid displacement. Eligibility Requirements Apply Funding is limited and assistance is subject to program guidelines, and income eligibility requirements. Moving Expenses Security Deposit Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nThursday, August 6, 2026\n\nTime\n\n12:30 PM - 1:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED\n\nStronger, Safer, Smarter: Injury Prevention for Athletes\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nJoin experts from White Plains Hospital for an engaging discussion on practical strategies to prevent common sports injuries, enhance performance, and stay in…\n\nUncovering Westchester LGBTQ+ History: Virtual Program\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nJoin librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester…"
