      "text": "Join experts from White Plains Hospital for an engaging discussion on practical strategies to prevent common sports injuries, enhance performance, and stay in…\n\nLearning\n\nStronger, Safer, Smarter: Injury Prevention for Athletes\n\nJoin experts from White Plains Hospital for an engaging discussion on practical strategies to prevent common sports injuries, enhance performance, and stay in…\n\nAbout this event\n\nJoin experts from White Plains Hospital for an engaging discussion on practical strategies to prevent common sports injuries, enhance performance, and stay in the game longer. Topics will include proper warm-ups, strength and conditioning, recovery techniques, and guidance on when to seek medical care. Ideal for athletes, parents, and coaches. Presented by Dr. Muhammad S. Rizwan Physiatrist, Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation and Sports Medicine White Plains Hospital and Burke Rehabilitation Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, June 16, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nSuccessfully Navigating College Admissions\n\nSep 16, 2026\n\nWe are offering this Zoom presentation to help families of high school juniors, sophomores and freshmen better understand the college admissions process and…\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED\n\nUncovering Westchester LGBTQ+ History: Virtual Program\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nJoin librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester…"
