      "excerpt": "Join librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester…",
      "text": "Join librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester…\n\nLearning\n\nUncovering Westchester LGBTQ+ History: Virtual Program\n\nJoin librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester…\n\nAbout this event\n\nJoin librarian and researcher Allee Manning for a celebration and deep dive into some of the true stories of the LGBTQ+ individuals who shaped Westchester with their advocacy, art, and activism. Expect plenty of fun trivia and thoughtful research. This program takes place on Zoom and registration is required. Click here to register. The program is being presented in partnership with the Town of Pelham Public Library and several other Westchester Libraries. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, June 16, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED\n\nStronger, Safer, Smarter: Injury Prevention for Athletes\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nJoin experts from White Plains Hospital for an engaging discussion on practical strategies to prevent common sports injuries, enhance performance, and stay in…\n\nGeorge Washington Carver: Genius Behind The Peanut Man\n\nJun 18, 2026\n\nBorn in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century."
